CRASH-04: report a [CURVES] row with only the curve name

6.0.0 does not crash on a [CURVES] row with only the curve name, but it
ignores the row (or creates an empty curve from it) without a message.
Legacy table_readCurve() rejects such a row with ERROR 203 (too few
items), which the fixed 5.3.0 now reaches. Report it the same way.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-04_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/TablesHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/TablesHandler.cpp
index 63bbe19..dde685b 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/TablesHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/TablesHandler.cpp
@@ -275,6 +275,13 @@ void handle_curves(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& lines
         auto tok = Tokenizer::tokenize(pl.data);
         if (tok.empty()) continue;
 
+        // A row with only the curve name is too few items (legacy
+        // table_readCurve, ERR_ITEMS); v6 formerly ignored it silently.
+        if (tok.size() < 2) {
+            ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_ITEMS, tok[0]));
+            continue;
+        }
+
         const std::string& maybe_name = tok[0];
         bool is_new_table = false;
